The new checks protect acquisitions within the grace period, but the inode read and owner write still use the shared pathname after `mkdir`. I’m replaying a pause beyond the default 30-second grace to check whether the acquirer can resume into a successor’s directory. I’m also checking EXIT cleanup before the main lock’s traps are installed.

